  "contracts": [
    "Sorted low RAM, readonly data ROM and stable high RAM reference actual bus vectors; no unknown word is initialized for execution",
    "All five memory maps and request/partial/commit/reset phases retain independent interval and permission expectations",
    "During a map change only the intersection of stable data extents is granted; relocated X-to-P storage loses its X grant",
    "Real owner writes and ROM installation change the exact borrowed words/knowledge bytes; native stores initialize the same high RAM cell",
    "Unknown RAM/ROM, holes and readonly stores stop before effects and retain real owner refusals with bank/address/PC",
    "Paired CPU/bus restore moves storage allocations and rebinds before native writes",
    "Full read/write observers suppress direct grants; unclocked native cache rebinding retains each callback and restores native transfers after detachment",
    "The native RAM load retires before the real peripheral-store boundary, preserving actual BCR effects and unknown BIU refusals"
  ],
